  "findings": {
    "nonpersist_filter": "Standard non-LiteOS IsNeedToSave only accepts persist. prefix; WritePersistParam returns0 before save for this debug key. Batch traversal prefix and per-entry filter also exclude it. Do not generalize this rule to LiteOS branches.",
    "memory": "InitParamService calls InitParamWorkSpace(0); workspace files use /dev/__parameters__. GetSharedMem writer opens O_CREAT|O_RDWR|O_TRUNC, ftruncate and MAP_SHARED. Standard device init mounts /dev tmpfs if not already mounted. Fresh init recreates runtime workspace rather than preserving this nonpersistent write.",
    "freshboot_recovery": "Source-supported conditional restoration path: unchanged default/import/persistent inputs plus new boot and no subsequent writer should recreate absence. Exact postboot errNum106 is mandatory acceptance; source is not a guarantee against vendor/default/service redefinition. Restarting only the app/parent does not clear parameter-service state.",
    "default_files": "Normal standard init loads /proc/dsmm/developer, /system/etc/param/ohos_const and GetCfgFiles(etc/param) directories in reverse policy order with ONLY_ADD. Loader handles .para and .para.import and recursively imports target files.",
    "key_search": "Zero exact-key occurrences in outer captured base/startup/init report. Reader scanned bounded suffixes, skipped symlinks and files>2MB, and did not cover all vendor/product/generated configs or .para.import extension files. This is NOT a complete deployed-default absence proof.",
    "provider": "Current baseline cached shim pointer equals the exact actual library SystemReadParam symbol; provider-final.json contains arithmetic and raw-guard evidence."
  },
  "recovery_acceptance": [
    "Preserve original boot and exact get semantic NOT_FOUND106; transport_rc0 alone is insufficient.",
    "For this diagnostic window set only exact true after freshboot and before new JNI_OnLoad; candidate logging must prove true was consumed.",
    "Rollback original four files and execute the separately authorized freshboot; do not use empty/false/save or modify parameter backing files to simulate absence.",
    "After changed boot, param get must again report exact106 with retained command/stdout/stderr and transport status. Any returned value, permission/read error or malformed output refuses absence restoration.",
    "Verify original runtime identities and actual restored feed before unlock."
  ],
